WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:18.208
[rock music playing]

2
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:22.208
[woman] <i>We're all trying
to catch up with something.</i>

3
00:00:22.291 --> 00:00:23.851
<i>School, love, friends, family, classes.</i>

4
00:00:23.916 --> 00:00:26.125
PRIVATE LESSON

5
00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:28.750
<i>The list is long. Life is short.</i>

6
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:31.125
<i>Maybe being an adult is all about
trying to catch up.</i>

7
00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:34.791
<i>But what about the lessons in life?</i>

8
00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:36.291
<i>That's where I come in</i>

9
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:39.416
<i>and become the person
my pupils need the most.</i>

10
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.250
- Ah. Ekin, my art instructor.
- Nice to meet you...

11
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:43.833
<i>Quite literally.</i>

12
00:00:43.916 --> 00:00:46.000
Miss Asude, my life coach is here.

13
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:47.083
Hello, there...

14
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.458
<i>By the way, I'm Azra.
I instruct young people.</i>

15
00:00:50.541 --> 00:00:51.875
<i>And they choose the subject.</i>

16
00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:53.375
It'll only hurt for a second.

17
00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:54.458
Ow!

18
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.833
- Look. Check this out!
- How's it going?

19
00:00:57.916 --> 00:01:00.351
[Azra] <i>I don't think parents need
to know every single detail.</i>

20
00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:01.416
It's good.

21
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.660
[Azra] <i>At the end of the day,</i>

22
00:01:02.708 --> 00:01:06.041
<i>these are private lessons
between the youngsters and me.</i>

23
00:01:06.125 --> 00:01:08.750
WORLD UNIVERSITY

24
00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:11.458
[Turkish music playing]

25
00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:12.916
FINE ARTS CLUB

26
00:01:15.458 --> 00:01:17.541
CULINARY CLUB
MUSIC CLUB

27
00:01:17.625 --> 00:01:19.625
[woman vocalizing]

28
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:32.708
- [woman] Hi, what's going on?
- Hello, girls.

29
00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:34.041
[woman] Hey.

30
00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:40.000
Why is that idiot
dressed like that? [sighs]

31
00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:43.208
- And the name of the club is...
- What does that say? Immo... Emo?

32
00:01:43.291 --> 00:01:44.750
Yeah, that's right. Emo.

33
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:47.666
- Right. "Immortal Literaries Club."
- [chuckles]

34
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.666
What's so hard to read?

35
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.041
- Take it easy, girl.
- [laughs]

36
00:01:50.125 --> 00:01:51.375
Afife Jale!

37
00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:53.498
- Jale's her name.
- [chuckles] The girl's not well.

38
00:01:53.541 --> 00:01:54.541
Come on. Let's go.

39
00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:57.625
You... no, my name's Hande!

40
00:01:57.708 --> 00:01:59.875
And seriously,
none of you know Afife Jale?

41
00:01:59.958 --> 00:02:03.333
There's, uh, the cycling club,
the Erasmus club,

42
00:02:03.416 --> 00:02:05.833
and this is the Immortal Literaries Club!

43
00:02:05.916 --> 00:02:07.291
No literary interest anyone?

44
00:02:07.375 --> 00:02:08.975
- This girl's a lunatic.
- Lunatic, yeah.

45
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:13.125
[laughing]

46
00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:18.500
[woman] This is outrageous.

47
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:20.250
- [grunts]
- Hey, you.

48
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:23.708
- Hande?
- [Hande] Afife Jale!

49
00:02:24.791 --> 00:02:26.041
Ah, I didn't mean to.

50
00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:29.500
- [gasps]
- [door closes]

51
00:02:31.208 --> 00:02:32.208
[grunts]

52
00:02:34.041 --> 00:02:35.875
[sobbing]

53
00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:44.166
[woman laughing]

54
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:48.208
Oh, my God<i>, </i>Azra.
Seriously, you are like a miracle.

55
00:02:48.291 --> 00:02:49.833
Girl, if it weren't for you...

56
00:02:49.916 --> 00:02:52.156
- I would never be able to date Tibet.
- [woman 2 grunts]

57
00:02:52.208 --> 00:02:53.958
- You're right about that.
- [mutters]

58
00:02:54.041 --> 00:02:56.250
Easy, girls. Someone could hear you.

59
00:02:56.333 --> 00:02:58.767
- Oh, let them hear us.
- Who could hear us in the girls' room?

60
00:02:58.791 --> 00:03:01.750
- [Azra] Let's check.
- [woman] I don't care if anyone hears.

61
00:03:01.833 --> 00:03:03.541
You could use some advertisement.

62
00:03:03.625 --> 00:03:04.625
[knock on door]

63
00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:05.875
OUT OF ORDER

64
00:03:08.208 --> 00:03:09.833
- [woman chuckles] Oh.
- [Hande gasps]

65
00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:13.333
Look, it's out of order. No one's here.

66
00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:16.666
I mean,
if it weren't for your private lessons...

67
00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.791
"Tibet, what even are we?"
is what you would be asking, hon.

68
00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:20.791
Cansu, shut up!

69
00:03:20.875 --> 00:03:22.416
- [Cansu scoffs]
- [exhales]

70
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.375
Oh, how he came crawling to me!

71
00:03:24.458 --> 00:03:26.708
I almost said he's gonna cry.

72
00:03:26.791 --> 00:03:30.750
You know what?
You've literally become my image maker.

73
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:33.333
When you called the chancellor
as my mom, I died.

74
00:03:33.416 --> 00:03:35.541
I mean, you are just so talented.

75
00:03:35.625 --> 00:03:38.333
You're the best private tutor
I've ever had in my life.

76
00:03:38.416 --> 00:03:41.166
[Azra] Girls, stop making this a big deal.
Come on, let's go.

77
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.916
- It's not a big deal.
- [Cansu sighs]

78
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.041
Azra, you are literally
changing lives with your work.

79
00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.965
- [squeals]
- [Cansu] That's an understatement.

80
00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:50.416
[woman] Wait. Wait for me, guys.

81
00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:11.541
- I wanna have private lessons too.
- [gasps]

82
00:04:11.625 --> 00:04:13.333
- [Hande] I wanna be noticed.
- [exhales]

83
00:04:13.416 --> 00:04:14.958
My dream is to be Utku's girlfriend.

84
00:04:15.041 --> 00:04:17.041
What are you talking about? Who are you?

85
00:04:17.125 --> 00:04:20.166
[chuckles] Oh, hi, I'm Hande.
I overheard you talking in the restroom.

86
00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.583
So please, help me too. Please.

87
00:04:21.666 --> 00:04:24.125
So, first you sneakily listen
to our conversation,

88
00:04:24.208 --> 00:04:26.500
then you jump out
of nowhere like a maniac,

89
00:04:26.583 --> 00:04:27.875
and now you want me to help you?

90
00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:30.791
- Yeah, that's right. [chuckles]
- Honey, have a good life.

91
00:04:30.875 --> 00:04:33.125
["Sana Ne" by Karsu playing]

92
00:04:38.541 --> 00:04:40.791
[Azra singing in Turkish]

93
00:04:47.041 --> 00:04:49.041
[continues singing]

94
00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.541
- [shouts]
- Azra, watch the road! Watch the road!

95
00:04:56.625 --> 00:04:59.065
I can't even watch movie scenes
when they stare while driving.

96
00:04:59.125 --> 00:05:01.458
- Get out of here.
- No, stop. I won't get out here!

97
00:05:01.541 --> 00:05:03.708
- [Azra] We'll see about that!
- [Hande] I won't!

98
00:05:05.708 --> 00:05:06.541
[sighs]

99
00:05:06.625 --> 00:05:08.791
- [laughing]
- [groans]

100
00:05:10.458 --> 00:05:12.666
You are something else, girl.
Do you even realize that?

101
00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.208
Should I call the cops?

102
00:05:14.291 --> 00:05:17.226
- I have your phone right here.
- What is it exactly that you want from me?

103
00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:20.500
Well, I want the exact same lesson
you've been teaching Melis.

104
00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:23.166
- Hmm.
- You know, the image maker.

105
00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.791
Or rather, making a boy recognize you
type lesson. Yeah, all of that.

106
00:05:26.875 --> 00:05:28.976
- But I'm not...
- And don't try to deny it. I heard it.

107
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.166
Melis said who knows
how many lives you've changed,

108
00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.416
and you didn't object,
so that means there are others.

109
00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:36.541
Oh, we have a smart ass here, I see.
What a surprise.

110
00:05:36.625 --> 00:05:37.958
That was honestly uncalled for.

111
00:05:38.041 --> 00:05:39.666
Oh, I'm sorry. What you just did wasn't?

112
00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.083
Come on.

113
00:05:43.041 --> 00:05:46.333
Come on. Hey, Azra, come on, please.

114
00:05:46.416 --> 00:05:49.041
- Please, please, please.
- All right, open the door. We'll talk.

115
00:05:49.125 --> 00:05:51.750
You can have this back then. [laughing]

116
00:05:54.458 --> 00:05:56.041
- [Azra sighs]
- [chuckles]

117
00:05:56.833 --> 00:05:57.750
[Azra gasps]

118
00:05:57.833 --> 00:05:59.333
Here you go.

119
00:05:59.416 --> 00:06:01.851
I was gonna snitch you out
to my aunt if you wouldn't help me.

120
00:06:01.875 --> 00:06:03.375
You'd snitch me out to your aunt?

121
00:06:03.458 --> 00:06:06.291
[chuckles] What's wrong with you?
Are you five years old?

122
00:06:07.083 --> 00:06:09.500
Call her,
tell her I said hi while you're at it.

123
00:06:10.833 --> 00:06:12.083
Because I'm not gonna help you.

124
00:06:12.875 --> 00:06:15.166
- [chuckles]
- Okay, as you wish.

125
00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.333
- [line ringing]
- [Azra sighs]

126
00:06:19.416 --> 00:06:20.250
[woman] <i>Hande?</i>

127
00:06:20.333 --> 00:06:22.041
How are you, aunty dearest?

128
00:06:22.125 --> 00:06:23.375
<i>What was that look about today?</i>

129
00:06:23.458 --> 00:06:25.750
<i>I couldn't say anything
with all the students around.</i>

130
00:06:25.833 --> 00:06:27.708
Yeah, we'll talk about that later.

131
00:06:27.791 --> 00:06:30.541
There's something very important
I want to tell you.

132
00:06:30.625 --> 00:06:32.666
<i>Make it quick, Hande. I'm very busy.</i>

133
00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:34.541
Yeah, I know. You're right.

134
00:06:34.625 --> 00:06:37.000
It's not easy being
the chancellor now, is it?

135
00:06:37.083 --> 00:06:38.934
<i>- Honey, we can talk later, huh?</i>
- Who said that?

136
00:06:38.958 --> 00:06:41.375
<i>All right, I have to go. See you.</i>

137
00:06:41.458 --> 00:06:42.791
- Give me that!
<i>- Bye, baby.</i>

138
00:06:42.875 --> 00:06:44.083
- [Azra grunting]
- Ow, ow!

139
00:06:44.166 --> 00:06:48.125
- Gimme that! [panting]
- No! Whoa, whoa!

140
00:06:48.208 --> 00:06:49.916
- Pulling hairs?
- Hmm.

141
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.625
What's wrong with you? Are you five?

142
00:06:52.208 --> 00:06:53.208
[Azra exhales]

143
00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.625
So, you're the niece
of the new chancellor.

144
00:06:56.708 --> 00:06:58.041
[Hande] Mm-hmm.

145
00:06:58.125 --> 00:07:01.333
I'm just trying to understand here.
What were you gonna tell your aunt anyway?

146
00:07:01.416 --> 00:07:04.791
That you were basically sneaking around
the college and among the actual students.

147
00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:07.458
So, you're a wise ass.
And the first one I meet here.

148
00:07:07.541 --> 00:07:10.666
Astonishing.
You're like Afife Sherlock Holmes.

149
00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.916
[Hande] Don't underestimate
my Holmesy charm.

150
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.208
[Azra] Enough with the puns.

151
00:07:15.208 --> 00:07:17.500
Here, take that. What's inside that?

152
00:07:17.583 --> 00:07:20.541
- Yo, careful with that box over there.
- [horn honking]

153
00:07:20.625 --> 00:07:21.708
God help me.

154
00:07:23.291 --> 00:07:26.083
What the hell! These people
have blocked the whole road.

155
00:07:26.583 --> 00:07:28.916
Hey, careful. Careful not to break that.

156
00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Hey, bro.

157
00:07:30.458 --> 00:07:32.166
[panting]

158
00:07:33.333 --> 00:07:34.750
You blocked the whole street.

159
00:07:34.833 --> 00:07:37.500
At least move those boxes,
so we can get inside.

160
00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:41.083
Hmm. Hold your horses, sister.

161
00:07:41.166 --> 00:07:43.125
Don't worry.
Building's not going anywhere.

162
00:07:43.208 --> 00:07:44.500
[Hande laughs]

163
00:07:45.291 --> 00:07:46.291
[Azra scoffs]

164
00:07:48.291 --> 00:07:49.291
[exhales]

165
00:07:59.083 --> 00:08:01.043
- Dude, move those boxes, will you?
- [both grunt]

166
00:08:01.083 --> 00:08:03.000
Come on, let these sisters get in!

167
00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:05.458
But what's going on?

168
00:08:06.208 --> 00:08:07.208
[Hande] Hmm.

169
00:08:08.208 --> 00:08:09.848
Gonna sneak into my place as well, Hande?

170
00:08:09.875 --> 00:08:11.995
Oh, of course not.
I'll just come back in the morning.

171
00:08:12.041 --> 00:08:15.166
Okay, fine.
Oh, not a word to your aunt about this.

172
00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:16.875
No, never. My lips are sealed.

173
00:08:18.125 --> 00:08:20.250
Yeah. Laters. Oh, which floor?

174
00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:21.583
- Which floor?
- [Azra] Second.

175
00:08:21.666 --> 00:08:23.250
Yeah, got it, second.

176
00:08:28.208 --> 00:08:30.166
What the heck's this now? [scoffs]

177
00:08:33.333 --> 00:08:34.666
[grunting]

178
00:08:37.958 --> 00:08:39.375
Excuse me!

179
00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.458
Um, anybody listening?

180
00:08:44.583 --> 00:08:46.875
Ugh. [exhales]

181
00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:55.125
[gasps]

182
00:08:55.208 --> 00:08:56.375
Oh, God, sorry.

183
00:08:57.291 --> 00:08:58.291
[grunts]

184
00:09:01.125 --> 00:09:02.445
Welcome to the building, I guess.

185
00:09:03.125 --> 00:09:05.666
Hello, sister. Who are you looking for?

186
00:09:07.625 --> 00:09:09.625
- It's you...
- Burak.

187
00:09:11.958 --> 00:09:14.198
Apartment three isn't
the best place to drop your things.

188
00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.250
- [Burak] Hmm.
- Downstairs.

189
00:09:16.333 --> 00:09:19.166
Oh, but of course,
you can't even see the number.

190
00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:23.125
Would you please move the cupboard?
It'd be great to get into my place.

191
00:09:23.208 --> 00:09:25.708
Uh, I'm sorry, but I can't right now.

192
00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.000
Oh? When do you think you can?

193
00:09:28.083 --> 00:09:31.625
Hmm, not sure.
You'll just have to wait, sis.

194
00:09:43.416 --> 00:09:46.541
Come in, man. Yeah, over here.

195
00:09:47.791 --> 00:09:49.791
[huffs] Sis. Oh, my God.

196
00:09:55.125 --> 00:09:56.125
[chuckles]

197
00:10:13.625 --> 00:10:16.625
- ["Are You Ready" by BBF playing, muffled]
<i>- ♪ Are you ready? ♪</i>

198
00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:19.333
<i>♪ Are you ready... ♪</i>

199
00:10:19.416 --> 00:10:21.416
[woman laughing, muffled]

200
00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:24.833
- [laughing continues]
- [groans]

201
00:10:27.083 --> 00:10:28.208
[huffs]

202
00:10:28.791 --> 00:10:30.750
<i>♪ Are you ready... ♪</i>

203
00:10:32.166 --> 00:10:33.166
[sighs]

204
00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:37.625
<i>♪ Are you ready, ready, ready... ♪</i>

205
00:10:37.708 --> 00:10:39.708
[knock on door]

206
00:10:43.791 --> 00:10:45.083
Good morning.

207
00:10:45.166 --> 00:10:46.916
Oh, my God, I forgot all about you.

208
00:10:47.416 --> 00:10:50.166
- [grunting]
- Mercury retrograde is really going down.

209
00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.750
- More like a meteor.
- [gasps]

210
00:10:51.833 --> 00:10:54.583
- Huh? What was that?
- Crashed all the way down.

211
00:10:56.541 --> 00:10:58.341
- Yeah, I don't really follow.
- [door closes]

212
00:10:58.375 --> 00:11:01.708
Yeah, my point exactly.
And you want private lessons now?

213
00:11:01.791 --> 00:11:04.250
Actually, I'd say
I'm very good with lessons.

214
00:11:04.333 --> 00:11:06.958
See, I did a little research
before I came here.

215
00:11:07.041 --> 00:11:08.041
That's a little for you?

216
00:11:08.083 --> 00:11:09.708
Indeed. So here it goes.

217
00:11:09.791 --> 00:11:10.958
<i>The Art of Picking Up Men.</i>

218
00:11:11.041 --> 00:11:13.708
<i>Women and Men.
A Time for You, a Time for a Change.</i>

219
00:11:13.791 --> 00:11:17.500
However, I don't think it's actually about
changing, because at the end of the day...

220
00:11:17.583 --> 00:11:18.583
Hande.

221
00:11:18.625 --> 00:11:19.458
Uh-huh. Yeah.

222
00:11:19.541 --> 00:11:20.583
Slow down, honey.

223
00:11:20.666 --> 00:11:23.708
- [exhales]
- Easy. Easy. Coffee?

224
00:11:23.791 --> 00:11:25.416
No, I can't have coffee.

225
00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.625
Coffee makes me very vivacious.
Then I talk too much.

226
00:11:27.708 --> 00:11:29.892
- Stimulants have that effect on...
- All right, got it.

227
00:11:29.916 --> 00:11:32.000
- Chamomile tea then.
- Tea is good.

228
00:11:32.083 --> 00:11:33.892
- [music continues, muffled]
- [woman laughing]

229
00:11:33.916 --> 00:11:35.208
[Hande exhales]

230
00:11:35.291 --> 00:11:36.291
[woman laughing] Stop!

231
00:11:36.875 --> 00:11:39.625
[Burak] Yes, you're amazing.
Yeah, you look stunning.

232
00:11:40.708 --> 00:11:42.625
- [camera shutter clicking]
- Keep your chin up.

233
00:11:44.416 --> 00:11:48.208
Perfect. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

234
00:11:48.291 --> 00:11:50.625
Okay, now gimme that big laugh.

235
00:11:50.708 --> 00:11:52.708
[woman laughing]

236
00:11:52.791 --> 00:11:57.083
Why do you think
everyone looks at me like I'm old?

237
00:11:57.833 --> 00:12:01.166
I mean, not that I'm gonna live
worrying about what people think.

238
00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:04.125
- Kids sold their souls to social media.
- [woman laughing]

239
00:12:04.208 --> 00:12:06.309
- [Azra sighs]
- That's not even an identity, you know.

240
00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:08.416
It's like an avatar existence.

241
00:12:10.208 --> 00:12:13.958
Uh, I mean, what they have online
is like an avatar existence.

242
00:12:14.458 --> 00:12:16.500
But am I like that? No, sir.

243
00:12:16.583 --> 00:12:19.250
You know, I like
to think that I have my own sty...

244
00:12:19.333 --> 00:12:21.916
[grunting]

245
00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.500
[huffs]

246
00:12:25.208 --> 00:12:26.250
[grunting]

247
00:12:26.333 --> 00:12:27.666
You can't be serious.

248
00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:31.125
If I'm the one who's old,
wait until they see you.

249
00:12:31.208 --> 00:12:33.125
Look at you. You're like an old hag.

250
00:12:33.791 --> 00:12:35.458
- [Azra sighs]
- Yeah.

251
00:12:38.041 --> 00:12:39.833
Okay, but I don't think I look old, right?

252
00:12:39.916 --> 00:12:41.208
Do I look old?

253
00:12:41.708 --> 00:12:43.791
What if that's what Utku sees, Azra? Huh?

254
00:12:43.875 --> 00:12:46.515
- Why did you, out of the blue...
- What did you mean by stimulant?

255
00:12:46.583 --> 00:12:50.041
- It's an arouser. I mean, for example...
- And what's with the ugly outfit, huh?

256
00:12:50.833 --> 00:12:51.916
Well, I'm comfortable.

257
00:12:52.625 --> 00:12:55.500
You don't need comfort, Hande.
You can be comfortable when you're old.

258
00:12:57.375 --> 00:12:59.708
- Are you a little on the edge?
- Not really. Why?

259
00:12:59.791 --> 00:13:02.083
You're acting passive-aggressive.
That's why I'm asking.

260
00:13:02.166 --> 00:13:04.500
Looks like you can confront Utku,
since you're so smart.

261
00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:06.625
Threatening someone
to work for you isn't great.

262
00:13:06.708 --> 00:13:08.208
I can be active-aggressive if I want.

263
00:13:08.291 --> 00:13:09.875
Okay, I'm sorry.

264
00:13:09.958 --> 00:13:11.208
I'm sorry.

265
00:13:12.166 --> 00:13:14.625
But you're the only one who can help me.

266
00:13:15.208 --> 00:13:18.750
I will not leave your doorstep unless
you help me. You know that, don't you?

267
00:13:18.833 --> 00:13:22.166
- This is exhausting.
- Please. Azra, please!

268
00:13:22.875 --> 00:13:26.583
Look at it this way. I wouldn't threaten
you if I weren't really desperate.

269
00:13:28.833 --> 00:13:30.833
[hangers clattering]

270
00:13:32.541 --> 00:13:33.541
[grunts]

271
00:13:35.166 --> 00:13:36.041
SCHEDULE

272
00:13:36.125 --> 00:13:38.416
Wow! She's really working.

273
00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.000
Is there a name
for this kind of work you're doing?

274
00:13:42.208 --> 00:13:44.000
I bet there's good money in this.

275
00:13:44.083 --> 00:13:46.916
Hey, stop it!
That is none of your business.

276
00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.000
Hmm.

277
00:13:48.958 --> 00:13:49.958
[Azra huffs]

278
00:13:54.916 --> 00:13:56.625
YOUR DREAMS ARE ONE CLICK AWAY

279
00:13:56.708 --> 00:13:58.833
[Hande] Why would anyone
choose this as a profession?

280
00:13:58.916 --> 00:14:00.875
Are you healing from past traumas or what?

281
00:14:00.958 --> 00:14:02.638
- [computer beeps]
- You have a new client.

282
00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:06.166
- Hey, Azra, you have a new client!
- What the hell are you doing?

283
00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:08.916
- Ow!
- Haven't you ever heard of boundaries?

284
00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:12.250
- So this is how people find you.
- [exhales]

285
00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:13.933
I would have sent you a message as well.

286
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.000
- Oh.
- You didn't have to make a fuss about it.

287
00:14:16.083 --> 00:14:20.000
You think you just book an appointment?
You need someone to recommend you.

288
00:14:20.583 --> 00:14:23.333
- [scoffs]
- I bet my aunt would recommend me.

289
00:14:23.416 --> 00:14:24.250
[Azra exhales]

290
00:14:24.333 --> 00:14:26.625
Or even, what... what was that girl's name?

291
00:14:26.708 --> 00:14:28.000
Wait, wait a second.

292
00:14:28.083 --> 00:14:29.916
Don't tell me. Oh, right.

293
00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.250
Melis. I bet she'd recommend me as well.

294
00:14:32.333 --> 00:14:34.041
Remember?
You called my aunt as her parent.

295
00:14:35.583 --> 00:14:36.416
Okay, fine.

296
00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:39.000
I got it. I can't get rid of you.

297
00:14:41.291 --> 00:14:43.250
There's a party at Utku's place tonight.

298
00:14:43.333 --> 00:14:45.500
- I don't know if you've heard about it.
- I haven't.

299
00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.791
- Let's start with that then.
- [laughs]

300
00:14:48.875 --> 00:14:52.666
Rule number one,
you will do exactly as I tell you.

301
00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:53.666
Exactly. I promise.

302
00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.416
- Second, books can't teach you about life.
- Mm-hmm.

303
00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.916
You need experience.
And get rid of that nonsense.

304
00:15:00.166 --> 00:15:01.166
[Hande] Hmm.

305
00:15:02.083 --> 00:15:03.625
[exhales]

306
00:15:03.708 --> 00:15:06.708
I just need experience.

307
00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:10.666
[gasps, grunts]

308
00:15:11.875 --> 00:15:12.875
[exhales]

309
00:15:14.791 --> 00:15:17.375
You're sure your aunt won't come home.
I don't wanna get busted.

310
00:15:17.458 --> 00:15:18.858
She's never there this time of day.

311
00:15:18.916 --> 00:15:21.666
[woman, muffled] Wow, Burak,
you kept me up all night. I'm exhausted.

312
00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:24.392
[Burak] Don't mention it.
Just tell me your schedule for next week...

313
00:15:24.416 --> 00:15:26.708
- [laughs] Oh.
- Hey!

314
00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.708
Hello, this cupboard is still out here.

315
00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.875
Wow, apartment three. Good morning.

316
00:15:41.958 --> 00:15:44.708
I totally forgot about that cupboard.
I'm sorry.

317
00:15:44.791 --> 00:15:47.916
They told me someone from the building
was complaining about the truck,

318
00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.840
so, you know,
I had to send the guys off early.

319
00:15:49.875 --> 00:15:51.958
That's the most pathetic apology
I've ever heard.

320
00:15:52.041 --> 00:15:54.958
Look, look, you can see
that I'm really busy right now.

321
00:15:55.041 --> 00:15:57.081
I'll get it moved once I finished.
Promise. See you.

322
00:15:57.125 --> 00:15:58.166
[Azra gasps]

323
00:16:02.208 --> 00:16:03.208
Seriously?

324
00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:07.958
- Oh, God.
- Stunning. She's like a work of art.

325
00:16:08.625 --> 00:16:10.416
Indeed. Just like you are.

326
00:16:11.291 --> 00:16:13.875
You shouldn't be so harsh
on people this early in the day.

327
00:16:13.958 --> 00:16:14.833
Why? What's it to you?

328
00:16:14.916 --> 00:16:16.916
I had an ounce of hope,
and now it's gone too.

329
00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.583
- [sighs]
- Why would Utku like me?

330
00:16:19.666 --> 00:16:23.083
They're women too,
so I... must be another species.

331
00:16:23.166 --> 00:16:25.958
That's for sure,
but I don't think you saw them clearly.

332
00:16:26.041 --> 00:16:27.875
The second girl had cheap breast implants.

333
00:16:27.958 --> 00:16:29.708
But her under-eye fillers were not so bad.

334
00:16:31.041 --> 00:16:33.250
The first girl's boots
were so out of style.

335
00:16:33.333 --> 00:16:36.041
And her hair was burnt,
probably from straightening it too much.

336
00:16:36.125 --> 00:16:39.000
I'm pretty sure she can't
even brush it through at this point.

337
00:16:39.083 --> 00:16:42.125
Anyway, listen, Hande,
we need to be quick.

338
00:16:42.208 --> 00:16:43.458
Come on, hurry up.

339
00:16:43.541 --> 00:16:46.416
We've got a lot of work to do
before the party, and trust me, a lot.

340
00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.958
- So many people are coming and going...
- Hande!

341
00:16:49.041 --> 00:16:51.375
[gasps, groans]

342
00:16:53.541 --> 00:16:55.916
- Welcome.
- [sighs]

343
00:16:58.541 --> 00:17:00.291
- Hi, my cutie!
- [cat meows]

344
00:17:06.666 --> 00:17:08.791
NAZIM HİKMET
NEW POEMS, TALES

345
00:17:11.125 --> 00:17:12.125
Huh.

346
00:17:21.583 --> 00:17:23.458
How long have you been living
with your aunt?

347
00:17:24.541 --> 00:17:25.958
She's the one who raised me.

348
00:17:26.541 --> 00:17:28.684
Let's go to my room.
I got some amazing things to show.

349
00:17:28.708 --> 00:17:30.333
- Let's go then.
- Okay.

350
00:17:32.583 --> 00:17:33.583
Come in.

351
00:17:36.291 --> 00:17:37.291
See?

352
00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:38.833
I've got great stuff.

353
00:17:38.916 --> 00:17:40.625
Why would we need to buy new clothes now?

354
00:17:42.166 --> 00:17:43.833
Kids out there are starving.

355
00:17:46.291 --> 00:17:48.166
Seriously, how old are you, Hande?

356
00:17:48.958 --> 00:17:53.416
I mean, if you've set your eyes on Utku,
we've got a lot of ground to cover.

357
00:17:54.541 --> 00:17:55.708
Is it that bad?

358
00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:58.656
Well, is the object
of your desire really open for debate?

359
00:17:59.666 --> 00:18:02.208
[exhales] I'm positive
I wanna be with him.

360
00:18:04.583 --> 00:18:05.791
You and I are going shopping.

361
00:18:05.875 --> 00:18:08.916
[gasps] But we have
something important we need to do first.

362
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.083
- Come on.
- We have something important to do.

363
00:18:11.166 --> 00:18:13.041
[chancellor] Look,
this is a revised version.

364
00:18:13.125 --> 00:18:15.333
This won't do, dear.
You need to rewrite it.

365
00:18:16.791 --> 00:18:17.791
What... what's that?

366
00:18:17.833 --> 00:18:21.291
[chancellor] No, I'm not going to
sign this. This is not the way to do this.

367
00:18:21.791 --> 00:18:22.951
Really, this is uncalled for.

368
00:18:24.041 --> 00:18:27.333
What can I say, Hande, baby, really, what?
This is unexpected of you.

369
00:18:27.916 --> 00:18:31.416
And it is also out of the blue,
this whole private lesson thing.

370
00:18:31.958 --> 00:18:33.750
The other day she called me.
She was excited.

371
00:18:33.833 --> 00:18:36.250
But I couldn't speak,
because I was very busy,

372
00:18:36.333 --> 00:18:39.500
and it got lost in the shuffle.
All right, dear, that'll be all.

373
00:18:40.375 --> 00:18:42.541
Oh, you're a fan of Yıldız Kenter?

374
00:18:42.625 --> 00:18:43.541
Excuse me.

375
00:18:43.625 --> 00:18:44.916
Oh, oh!

376
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.125
Right. I was a pupil of hers, actually.

377
00:18:47.208 --> 00:18:48.416
[chancellor] Hmm.

378
00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:51.625
Though that
wasn't my major when I studied.

379
00:18:52.125 --> 00:18:54.791
In fact,
I'm a graduate student of your college.

380
00:18:54.875 --> 00:18:56.625
- You went here?
- [Azra] Yeah.

381
00:18:56.708 --> 00:19:00.125
Even though theater
has always been my real passion.

382
00:19:00.208 --> 00:19:01.728
[chuckles] Thanks to my tutor, Yıldız.

383
00:19:01.791 --> 00:19:03.958
That's unbelievable. Wonderful.

384
00:19:04.041 --> 00:19:05.750
- Great. Hande, listen.
- Hmm.

385
00:19:05.833 --> 00:19:08.791
If you had told me this from the get-go,
things would be a lot different.

386
00:19:08.875 --> 00:19:11.458
She's obsessed with standups,
but what good will that do, right?

387
00:19:11.541 --> 00:19:14.250
[laughs] You need to have
a solid foundation, right, Azra?

388
00:19:14.333 --> 00:19:17.416
Well, aunty, of course
it's not easy to be as perceptive

389
00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.041
and astute as you are.

390
00:19:19.125 --> 00:19:21.205
I mean, it takes time,
but I'll get there eventually.

391
00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:24.833
But now that I have the amazing Azra,
she will help me reach my dreams.

392
00:19:24.916 --> 00:19:27.125
By realizing your potential,
yeah, exactly,

393
00:19:27.208 --> 00:19:31.250
but it's always important
to set the right goals for yourself.

394
00:19:31.333 --> 00:19:33.351
- That's so true.
- [chancellor] You got that right.

395
00:19:33.375 --> 00:19:36.125
- Bravo! And, Hande, good job to you, baby.
- [Hande] Oh.

396
00:19:36.208 --> 00:19:37.833
- [chancellor] You're amazing.
- Stop it!

397
00:19:37.916 --> 00:19:40.333
[chancellor] Well, then, good luck to you.

398
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:44.083
- Oh! [chuckles]
- Well, never mind, I'll get it some way.

399
00:19:44.166 --> 00:19:46.208
- I guess.
- Oh, but by the way.

400
00:19:46.291 --> 00:19:49.916
I'm was thinking of taking Hande
to the Nazım Hikmet Oratorio tonight.

401
00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.125
Just for starters.

402
00:19:51.208 --> 00:19:52.791
<i>With your permission, of course.</i>

403
00:19:52.875 --> 00:19:56.000
<i>And so I might
drop Hande off a little late tonight.</i>

404
00:19:56.083 --> 00:19:58.625
[chancellor] <i>Okay, but not too late.</i>

405
00:19:59.916 --> 00:20:01.041
Ready to get started?

406
00:20:01.791 --> 00:20:03.750
- Yes, please.
- Come on, then.

407
00:20:09.125 --> 00:20:12.250
- Inner beauty is important, Hande.
- [gasps] Oh, silly me.

408
00:20:12.333 --> 00:20:15.666
I thought the term inner beauty
was referring to the soul. [laughs]

409
00:20:17.291 --> 00:20:19.458
Azra! [gasps]

410
00:20:19.541 --> 00:20:22.125
Oh, my God. I have boobs!
Wait a second. Wait, wait.

411
00:20:23.791 --> 00:20:26.666
Azra, I can't believe it.
They're literally like 3D!

412
00:20:27.333 --> 00:20:31.041
Azra? Azra, let me ask you.
What do you think about...

413
00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.708
[Azra] All right,
now it's time for makeup.

414
00:20:33.791 --> 00:20:36.916
[Hande] Come on, don't underestimate me.
Even I have a makeup bag.

415
00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.083
It was a sample.
Hang on, uh, let me show it to you.

416
00:20:39.166 --> 00:20:42.666
- And what's inside it?
- Um, lipstick, blush, mascara.

417
00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:43.916
Uh-huh.

418
00:20:44.416 --> 00:20:45.291
[Hande hesitates]

419
00:20:45.375 --> 00:20:48.250
Why? What else should there be?
I'm gonna leave that here.

420
00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:51.333
Come on, Hande, let's go.

421
00:20:52.791 --> 00:20:55.458
- Hey, Azra! Oh, I just love...
- [Azra sighs]

422
00:21:01.041 --> 00:21:02.958
Azra. [laughing]

423
00:21:07.375 --> 00:21:08.375
Azra.

424
00:21:09.625 --> 00:21:10.625
[chuckles]

425
00:21:11.541 --> 00:21:12.541
[both laugh]

426
00:21:12.583 --> 00:21:14.666
[dance music playing]

427
00:21:23.041 --> 00:21:24.083
He looked.

428
00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:26.833
Utku Atalan has just looked at me,

429
00:21:26.916 --> 00:21:28.916
so I'm going home,
because I can't do this.

430
00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:31.583
Hande, stop being silly.
You can be shocked later.

431
00:21:31.666 --> 00:21:33.375
But now it's time for action. Move.

432
00:21:33.458 --> 00:21:34.666
Wait, I can't walk down.

433
00:21:42.791 --> 00:21:45.333
- [Cansu] Hey!
- Hi!

434
00:21:45.416 --> 00:21:47.458
- How you doing, ladies?
- Good!

435
00:21:48.458 --> 00:21:51.250
- New pupil?
- Correct, and it's all thanks to you.

436
00:21:51.333 --> 00:21:53.809
- What's that supposed to mean?
- She's the chancellor's niece.

437
00:21:53.833 --> 00:21:55.458
- No! Wow. [chuckles]
- [Azra] Mm-hmm.

438
00:21:55.541 --> 00:21:57.833
- [Melis gasps]
- She eavesdropped on us in the restroom.

439
00:21:57.916 --> 00:21:59.750
What were you talking about
in the restroom?

440
00:21:59.833 --> 00:22:01.625
Nothing, just, you know, girl stuff.

441
00:22:01.708 --> 00:22:04.559
Anyway, let's drink up. Come on,
live it up. We're at a party, aren't we?

442
00:22:04.583 --> 00:22:06.791
Love that for us! Here, girl.

443
00:22:12.041 --> 00:22:14.750
- [laughing]
- [Hande coughs]

444
00:22:14.833 --> 00:22:15.916
Enjoy it, girls.

445
00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:18.750
[dance music continues playing]

446
00:22:21.208 --> 00:22:25.291
- Yes! Give it to me! Yes!
- Ah. And she hacks yet another password.

447
00:22:25.375 --> 00:22:29.041
No, honey, your girl is no longer dealing
with petty little passwords.

448
00:22:29.125 --> 00:22:31.875
Listen to me. From now on,
it's international waters for me.

449
00:22:31.958 --> 00:22:34.458
Cansu, just be careful
and try not to get into trouble, okay?

450
00:22:34.541 --> 00:22:37.875
It would take us way too long to explain
to your mother what a hacker is.

451
00:22:37.958 --> 00:22:39.541
Oh, you can't even imagine.

452
00:22:39.625 --> 00:22:41.851
My mother literally still thinks
Facebook's the Internet.

453
00:22:41.875 --> 00:22:42.875
[both laugh]

454
00:22:43.833 --> 00:22:45.041
[Utku] Attention, people!

455
00:22:45.125 --> 00:22:48.250
<i>Señores, señoritas!</i>
Are we having fun, yet?

456
00:22:48.333 --> 00:22:50.250
[cheering]

457
00:22:50.333 --> 00:22:52.333
This guy is so full of himself.

458
00:22:52.416 --> 00:22:54.083
All right, as always,

459
00:22:54.166 --> 00:22:57.833
this sexy sombrero I'm wearing
will go to the king or queen

460
00:22:57.916 --> 00:23:00.666
who will have
the most tequila shots tonight!

461
00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:03.000
[cheering]

462
00:23:03.083 --> 00:23:04.791
[Utku] Let's bring on the shots!

463
00:23:04.875 --> 00:23:06.583
[dance music playing]

464
00:23:07.166 --> 00:23:09.416
Here you go, peeps! [laughs]

465
00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:10.916
- Yeah, come on!
- Whoo-hoo!

466
00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:12.875
[music continues]

467
00:23:18.791 --> 00:23:20.625
- Shots?
- [Melis] Whoo!

468
00:23:34.375 --> 00:23:36.583
[laughing]

469
00:23:38.125 --> 00:23:40.291
- [music continues]
- [laughing]

470
00:23:43.791 --> 00:23:45.833
- [laughing]
- [Hande] Azra!

471
00:23:46.541 --> 00:23:49.083
I'm having so much fun, you know.

472
00:23:49.166 --> 00:23:52.166
Right now, I'm so happy and... [laughing]

473
00:23:53.458 --> 00:23:56.041
Hande, I can see that,
but you need to get a hold of yourself.

474
00:23:56.125 --> 00:23:57.500
This is not good.

475
00:23:57.583 --> 00:23:58.916
Azra!

476
00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:02.250
Hey, I can't hear you, Azra.
It's too noisy in here.

477
00:24:02.333 --> 00:24:05.213
- And I can't understand anything.
- Let's throw some water on your face.

478
00:24:12.041 --> 00:24:14.291
- [Azra] Duygu.
- Azra.

479
00:24:15.125 --> 00:24:17.041
- Why... [sighs]
- What's up, Duygu?

480
00:24:17.125 --> 00:24:20.208
- Cenk, Azra. [sighs]
- Wow, Azra.

481
00:24:20.291 --> 00:24:21.166
I've heard about you.

482
00:24:21.250 --> 00:24:22.625
[Azra] Hmm.

483
00:24:22.708 --> 00:24:26.500
Well, I was just telling Duygu
she could crash at my place tonight.

484
00:24:26.583 --> 00:24:28.583
But she's saying
her family wouldn't let her.

485
00:24:28.666 --> 00:24:31.250
I heard you're an expert
at handling these things.

486
00:24:31.333 --> 00:24:33.625
- You need to leave the girl alone.
- Leave her alone?

487
00:24:33.708 --> 00:24:35.416
- Who do you think you are?
- We should go.

488
00:24:35.500 --> 00:24:38.000
- Come on, let's get out of here.
- Hang on a second.

489
00:24:39.083 --> 00:24:40.916
Hey, cover for us tonight, will you?

490
00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.208
Don't worry. I'll pay for your troubles.

491
00:24:43.708 --> 00:24:46.125
- [grunts]
- Yeah, wrong number, man. Get out!

492
00:24:46.208 --> 00:24:47.208
[Cenk gasps]

493
00:24:48.916 --> 00:24:49.916
[huffs]

494
00:24:50.666 --> 00:24:52.083
See what he wants from you?

495
00:24:52.166 --> 00:24:54.666
Do you even realize
how he's making you look?

496
00:24:54.750 --> 00:24:57.166
I've told you over and over again.
I warned you.

497
00:24:57.666 --> 00:24:58.875
Go home right now.

498
00:25:00.791 --> 00:25:02.708
- Do you have enough money for a cab?
- I do.

499
00:25:02.791 --> 00:25:05.750
- [dance music playing]
- Thank you so much, guys. Thank you.

500
00:25:05.833 --> 00:25:06.833
Whoo!

501
00:25:07.291 --> 00:25:09.708
[laughing] Yeah, yeah!

502
00:25:14.875 --> 00:25:17.083
That's right! Ooh! [laughing]

503
00:25:17.166 --> 00:25:19.458
Hande! Hande!

504
00:25:20.166 --> 00:25:22.750
Azra, I won the hat! Azra...

505
00:25:22.833 --> 00:25:26.208
Oh, Azra! Oh, Azra!

506
00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:46.250
Hey, wanna help?

507
00:25:46.333 --> 00:25:49.666
I was just looking for a pick and shovel.
So we can bury her.

508
00:25:51.791 --> 00:25:53.041
[both laugh]

509
00:25:54.666 --> 00:25:57.000
[Hande panting]

510
00:26:01.875 --> 00:26:03.750
[grunts] I can't believe
how stubborn you are.

511
00:26:03.833 --> 00:26:06.000
Look, this cupboard is still here.

512
00:26:06.083 --> 00:26:07.803
- You think I'm the stubborn one?
- [groans]

513
00:26:07.875 --> 00:26:09.355
You think I'm the one being stubborn?

514
00:26:09.416 --> 00:26:10.708
Look, it's already 11 p.m.

515
00:26:10.791 --> 00:26:13.541
I still need to take her home.
How are we going to get inside?

516
00:26:13.625 --> 00:26:16.166
[Burak] Is there someone at her place?
Why don't you ask her?

517
00:26:16.250 --> 00:26:18.458
I'm pretty sure you're up to something.
Never mind.

518
00:26:18.541 --> 00:26:21.666
What are you talking about?
No one's up to anything. [sighs]

519
00:26:21.750 --> 00:26:23.150
Whoa, whoa, be careful, be careful.

520
00:26:23.208 --> 00:26:26.500
- [grunts]
- And you've been eavesdropping on us.

521
00:26:27.708 --> 00:26:28.708
[Burak] Oh.

522
00:26:29.833 --> 00:26:30.750
[Hande groans]

523
00:26:30.833 --> 00:26:32.333
- [lock clicks]
- [Azra gasps]

524
00:26:34.291 --> 00:26:36.583
Oh, no. It's Makbule.
She's our local Mrs. Grundy.

525
00:26:37.750 --> 00:26:39.583
She's trying to eavesdrop on us.

526
00:26:39.666 --> 00:26:41.833
Oh! Like you.

527
00:26:41.916 --> 00:26:43.333
You two will get along.

528
00:26:43.958 --> 00:26:45.791
[chuckling]

529
00:26:45.875 --> 00:26:48.083
- [Hande groans]
- [Azra grunts]

530
00:26:48.166 --> 00:26:49.291
Look, stop being stubborn.

531
00:26:49.375 --> 00:26:51.375
We can't get in here,
so let's just go to my place.

532
00:26:51.416 --> 00:26:53.208
- [Azra] Nope.
- Come on!

533
00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:57.583
- Can you please locate the bed?
- [gasps] Shh! Hande! Shh!

534
00:26:57.666 --> 00:26:59.666
- [Hande] I need to lie down.
- Let's go to yours.

535
00:26:59.750 --> 00:27:02.333
- [Hande speaks muffled]
- Hande, quiet!

536
00:27:02.916 --> 00:27:06.583
Hey, I'm sorry the place is a mess.
I'm still getting settled in.

537
00:27:06.666 --> 00:27:08.706
[Azra] Oh, no.
We're so sorry to barge in like this.

538
00:27:08.750 --> 00:27:09.750
Thanks for the help.

539
00:27:09.791 --> 00:27:10.958
She's okay, right?

540
00:27:11.041 --> 00:27:13.750
- Hande, you're okay, right?
- [Hande] Yeah!

541
00:27:13.833 --> 00:27:16.208
- Okay. I'll make some coffee anyway.
- [chuckles]

542
00:27:18.458 --> 00:27:19.458
[sighs]

543
00:27:21.958 --> 00:27:23.583
Would you like some coffee as well?

544
00:27:23.666 --> 00:27:25.500
[Azra] Yeah, don't mind if I do.

545
00:27:32.333 --> 00:27:34.416
The whips are probably
in the bedroom. [scoffs]

546
00:27:35.875 --> 00:27:36.708
What's that you said?

547
00:27:36.791 --> 00:27:39.916
Uh, I said the neighbors are asleep,
I imagine.

548
00:27:46.375 --> 00:27:48.375
[water sloshing]

549
00:27:49.291 --> 00:27:52.708
- [Azra gasps] Hande! What are you doing?
- [Hande] Oh!

550
00:27:52.791 --> 00:27:55.642
- Get up. Stop, sweetie, just stop.
- Leave me alone! Hey, leave me alone!

551
00:27:55.666 --> 00:27:58.708
- Get up. [groans]
- I just wanted to wash up.

552
00:28:01.583 --> 00:28:02.708
This woman...

553
00:28:04.375 --> 00:28:07.083
- This Azra...
- Hmm.

554
00:28:07.166 --> 00:28:09.541
[Hande] ...she is the perfect woman.

555
00:28:09.625 --> 00:28:14.083
Because this woman
will set me up with Utku.

556
00:28:14.166 --> 00:28:15.041
But don't tell anyone.

557
00:28:15.125 --> 00:28:16.541
[Burak] Mm.

558
00:28:17.625 --> 00:28:19.305
- [Hande] This woman, amazing!
- [chuckles]

559
00:28:19.375 --> 00:28:20.375
[gasps]

560
00:28:22.083 --> 00:28:25.375
No, you don't know her.
You don't know her. No, no, no, sir.

561
00:28:25.458 --> 00:28:27.458
- [sighs]
- [Hande] But she can do it.

562
00:28:27.541 --> 00:28:29.125
She can do anything.

563
00:28:29.208 --> 00:28:31.041
- You don't know her yet.
- [clears throat]

564
00:28:31.125 --> 00:28:33.833
You're absolutely right.
I had no idea who she is.

565
00:28:33.916 --> 00:28:35.458
But...

566
00:28:36.041 --> 00:28:37.291
[Hande laughs]

567
00:28:37.375 --> 00:28:39.041
I know her name is Azra.

568
00:28:40.291 --> 00:28:42.125
I would love to get to know more though.

569
00:28:42.208 --> 00:28:43.541
[sighs]

570
00:28:43.625 --> 00:28:45.500
- Hey, listen, listen, listen. Listen.
- Huh.

571
00:28:45.583 --> 00:28:46.875
I'm Hande, by the way.

572
00:28:47.750 --> 00:28:48.833
That's me.

573
00:28:48.916 --> 00:28:51.666
But I've no idea
if it's one or two syllables.

574
00:28:51.750 --> 00:28:55.208
I mean, you can't really
expect me to know everything. [laughs]

575
00:28:55.291 --> 00:28:59.166
Hey, he's making me laugh!
He's making me laugh! [laughing]

576
00:28:59.250 --> 00:29:00.458
What exactly did she drink?

577
00:29:00.541 --> 00:29:02.708
Tequila, but I guess
it hit her like Absinthe.

578
00:29:02.791 --> 00:29:04.166
- The kid could use air.
- Choking.

579
00:29:04.250 --> 00:29:05.750
- Great idea.
- [Hande] I can't...

580
00:29:05.833 --> 00:29:07.892
- Wait, I'm telling you I can't breathe.
- [laughing]

581
00:29:07.916 --> 00:29:09.791
- [laughs] Wait!
- Up you go.

582
00:29:15.291 --> 00:29:18.291
- [Azra] Come here.
- [Hande sighs] Wow, this feels good.

583
00:29:18.375 --> 00:29:19.916
- [Azra] Take a breath.
- [Hande sighs]

584
00:29:21.833 --> 00:29:22.833
[exhales]

585
00:29:24.625 --> 00:29:25.625
[chuckles]

586
00:29:27.250 --> 00:29:29.125
You know, guys,

587
00:29:29.208 --> 00:29:31.250
I really thought I was gonna

588
00:29:32.625 --> 00:29:36.166
get old without ever dancing
or having a boyfriend.

589
00:29:36.250 --> 00:29:39.875
- [chuckling]
- You're such a blessing, Azra.

590
00:29:39.958 --> 00:29:41.083
Oh!

591
00:29:41.166 --> 00:29:42.666
Hmm.

592
00:29:42.750 --> 00:29:46.458
- You're such a blessing. Aww.
- [Azra chuckles]

593
00:29:46.541 --> 00:29:50.458
By the way, I don't think anyone even
realized that, but I was pretty drunk.

594
00:29:50.541 --> 00:29:52.250
And you don't even need that much.

595
00:29:52.333 --> 00:29:54.708
And you know, I'm done with that,
like, serious... oh.

596
00:29:54.791 --> 00:29:55.791
Coffee?

597
00:29:56.666 --> 00:29:59.625
- Coffee. Azra, are you sure about this?
- Yep, you'll feel better.

598
00:29:59.708 --> 00:30:01.333
- Are you sure?
- Yes, drink up.

599
00:30:01.416 --> 00:30:02.541
- [slurps]
- [chuckles]

600
00:30:04.708 --> 00:30:05.875
Whoa. Mm.

601
00:30:07.875 --> 00:30:10.625
That's weird.
Doesn't that car look like my aunt's car?

602
00:30:10.708 --> 00:30:11.708
[Azra] Huh?

603
00:30:11.750 --> 00:30:13.750
[fast-paced music playing]

604
00:30:16.291 --> 00:30:17.333
[chancellor] Thank you.

605
00:30:17.416 --> 00:30:18.625
What? Ülker?

606
00:30:18.708 --> 00:30:21.500
- What's Ülker doing here?
- Well, I texted her my location.

607
00:30:21.583 --> 00:30:22.416
[Azra gasps]

608
00:30:22.500 --> 00:30:25.500
Because, you know, I've been too much
of a burden for you today.

609
00:30:25.583 --> 00:30:28.208
Please, my apologies.
I thought I should be on my way.

610
00:30:28.291 --> 00:30:29.684
- Good for you, Hande!
- By the way.

611
00:30:29.708 --> 00:30:32.000
- [hesitates] About my aunt's car.
- [sighs] Stay here.

612
00:30:32.083 --> 00:30:34.750
Do you think the car looks like my aunt,
or my aunt...

613
00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:38.333
[grunts] ...looks like the car?
But that car's really...

614
00:30:42.333 --> 00:30:46.166
- Ooh!
- [Azra] Hey, grab one end. Grab one end.

615
00:30:46.250 --> 00:30:48.875
- What do you mean grab one end?
- [Azra sighs]

616
00:30:51.500 --> 00:30:54.583
- Hande, shh! Wait. Don't let her go.
- Wait, wait, wait, my sombrero!

617
00:30:54.666 --> 00:30:56.125
No, later. We'll come back for it.

618
00:30:56.208 --> 00:30:59.000
- Please let me find my sombrero. Please!
- We'll come later, okay?

619
00:30:59.083 --> 00:31:00.083
Quickly, quickly.

620
00:31:02.500 --> 00:31:04.458
Oh. The elevator.

621
00:31:08.375 --> 00:31:09.208
[gasping]

622
00:31:09.291 --> 00:31:12.208
Too late.
Upstairs, upstairs, upstairs, upstairs.

623
00:31:14.041 --> 00:31:16.375
- [sighs]
- [Ülker] Hande?

624
00:31:17.166 --> 00:31:19.333
Ülker, hello, there. Hello.

625
00:31:20.208 --> 00:31:21.791
- Oh, hello. Up here.
- Oh. Okay.

626
00:31:21.875 --> 00:31:23.375
[panting]

627
00:31:26.958 --> 00:31:29.333
[music playing over dialogue]

628
00:31:33.333 --> 00:31:36.125
Oh, my! [grunts]

629
00:31:36.208 --> 00:31:38.208
- Listen, here's what we're gonna do.
- Okay.

630
00:31:38.291 --> 00:31:40.291
We're gonna play a great game together.

631
00:31:40.375 --> 00:31:42.041
- Are you ready?
- I am. [chuckles]

632
00:31:42.125 --> 00:31:43.583
[both] Shh!

633
00:31:43.666 --> 00:31:47.416
- Hmm. Yes, hello. How are you, Azra?
- Hello, there.

634
00:31:47.500 --> 00:31:51.375
You're here. Yes, rightfully I must add,
to take Hande home with you.

635
00:31:51.458 --> 00:31:52.958
Because she called you.

636
00:31:54.166 --> 00:31:56.791
Um, did you find the place easily?

637
00:31:56.875 --> 00:31:58.083
Yeah, yeah, it was easy. Fine.

638
00:31:58.166 --> 00:32:00.208
- Great.
- Um, where's Hande, honey? Hande.

639
00:32:00.291 --> 00:32:02.583
Yes, I was just coming to that.

640
00:32:02.666 --> 00:32:05.416
Uh, where is Hande? [chuckles]

641
00:32:06.041 --> 00:32:08.541
Almost sounds like a play, right?
[inhales]

642
00:32:08.625 --> 00:32:10.958
Like, <i>For Whom the Bell Tolls</i>, right?

643
00:32:11.041 --> 00:32:12.708
- [chuckles]
- Yes. Uh, Hande!

644
00:32:12.791 --> 00:32:15.166
Why is she keeping me waiting
at the door? Why?

645
00:32:15.250 --> 00:32:16.083
Well.

646
00:32:16.166 --> 00:32:17.601
- [sighs] Hande dear.
- [Ülker] Hande!

647
00:32:17.625 --> 00:32:20.375
Oh! Hande's sleeping.

648
00:32:20.458 --> 00:32:22.083
- What?
- Well, she's asleep.

649
00:32:22.166 --> 00:32:24.541
We had a very long day.
She's fallen asleep.

650
00:32:24.625 --> 00:32:27.541
- What's all this about? This is unusual.
- Well...

651
00:32:27.625 --> 00:32:30.583
- Step aside, child. I need to see her.
- All right. [grunts]

652
00:32:35.000 --> 00:32:36.000
Hande.

653
00:32:37.375 --> 00:32:40.583
Hande, get up, baby, get up. Honey.

654
00:32:40.666 --> 00:32:42.500
Maybe we let her sleep.

655
00:32:42.583 --> 00:32:45.541
No, no. What could I do?
This is not good at all.

656
00:32:47.375 --> 00:32:48.208
I mean...

657
00:32:48.291 --> 00:32:49.583
Uh, we just moved in.

658
00:32:49.666 --> 00:32:52.500
- I hope you don't mind. Place is a mess.
- All right. All right.

659
00:32:54.791 --> 00:32:58.125
- [Azra gasps]
- Tell her to call me as soon as she wakes.

660
00:32:58.208 --> 00:33:00.208
- First thing.
- You can count on that. I promise.

661
00:33:00.291 --> 00:33:02.250
- Good night, then.
- Good night.

662
00:33:02.333 --> 00:33:06.375
Oh, dear, oh, dear.
This is so unusual of her. [grunts]

663
00:33:10.833 --> 00:33:12.250
[sighs]

664
00:33:14.333 --> 00:33:16.291
[grunts] Hey, what's up?

665
00:33:16.375 --> 00:33:17.750
[laughs] What is that?

666
00:33:17.833 --> 00:33:18.666
Is she gone?

667
00:33:18.750 --> 00:33:21.041
Yeah, yeah. Where's Hande?

668
00:33:25.458 --> 00:33:27.125
[chuckles] Shh!

669
00:33:28.083 --> 00:33:32.291
[laughs] Azra. Oh, my God.
I won! I won for real! I did!

670
00:33:32.375 --> 00:33:35.291
Let me. Let me.
Yep, you're right. You won.

671
00:33:35.375 --> 00:33:36.708
You're so good at the quiet game.

672
00:33:36.791 --> 00:33:39.166
- You really play it well.
- Hey, don't be a killjoy.

673
00:33:39.250 --> 00:33:42.833
- [laughs]
- By the way, that wig looks good on you.

674
00:33:42.916 --> 00:33:46.416
- Why, thank you.
- [laughing] Stop it.

675
00:33:46.500 --> 00:33:47.666
- Let's go.
- All right, fine.

676
00:33:47.750 --> 00:33:49.583
- I appreciate it.
- Thank you so much.

677
00:33:49.666 --> 00:33:50.666
[Burak chuckles]

678
00:33:56.416 --> 00:33:57.500
Okay, now... [sighs]

679
00:33:57.583 --> 00:33:58.583
...time to sleep.

680
00:33:59.416 --> 00:34:02.083
- I'll run back upstairs to grab our stuff.
- Uh-huh.

681
00:34:02.166 --> 00:34:04.583
- What?
- Oh, nothing.

682
00:34:04.666 --> 00:34:07.416
So, I was drunk.
I wasn't blind though, was I?

683
00:34:07.500 --> 00:34:10.083
- Hande!
- [laughs] Oh.

684
00:34:10.166 --> 00:34:12.333
- Go to sleep.
- Okay, good night.

685
00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:13.916
- Hey!
- [Azra exhales]

686
00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:16.166
Can you tell Burak I said hi, please?

687
00:34:17.875 --> 00:34:18.875
[lights click]

688
00:34:23.750 --> 00:34:24.750
[gasps]

689
00:34:27.208 --> 00:34:28.791
[exhales] Huh.

690
00:34:28.875 --> 00:34:30.291
Didn't finish your coffee.

691
00:34:31.041 --> 00:34:32.841
You could come back
and finish it if you want.

692
00:34:33.916 --> 00:34:37.083
Well, no, but I should go.

693
00:34:37.916 --> 00:34:42.000
But I came
because I need to get our things.

694
00:34:43.333 --> 00:34:44.583
So, I'll just go grab them.

695
00:34:44.666 --> 00:34:46.000
- [chuckles]
- Hmm.

696
00:34:48.583 --> 00:34:51.458
- [pop music playing]
- [sighs]

697
00:35:06.458 --> 00:35:08.458
[vocalizing]

698
00:35:22.708 --> 00:35:24.208
[Azra] <i>Now, here's our first subject.</i>

699
00:35:24.291 --> 00:35:26.291
How to attract guys.

700
00:35:26.375 --> 00:35:28.291
[laughing]

701
00:35:28.375 --> 00:35:30.875
What do you think
was Cinderella's biggest mistake?

702
00:35:31.666 --> 00:35:33.375
Duh. Giving in to her stepmother.

703
00:35:33.458 --> 00:35:36.916
No, choosing a guy
who only cared about appearances.

704
00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:38.125
[Hande] Oh.

705
00:35:39.916 --> 00:35:42.250
What... you just insinuate something?

706
00:35:42.333 --> 00:35:46.041
No, I'm just enlightening you. [scoffs]

707
00:35:47.041 --> 00:35:48.666
You need to find your own style.

708
00:35:49.541 --> 00:35:52.250
You always look down
on girls trying to be like pop stars

709
00:35:52.333 --> 00:35:54.250
while you're trying to be Afife Jale.

710
00:35:54.750 --> 00:35:57.125
I'm not judging the actual clothes
in your wardrobe,

711
00:35:57.625 --> 00:36:00.041
but you look like
an ancient author styled you.

712
00:36:00.125 --> 00:36:01.625
[Hande] Hmm. Hmm.

713
00:36:02.333 --> 00:36:03.833
Be yourself.

714
00:36:05.083 --> 00:36:06.083
Myself.

715
00:36:06.125 --> 00:36:07.125
Hello, there.

716
00:36:08.250 --> 00:36:09.416
Welcome.

717
00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:10.541
[Azra sighs]

718
00:36:12.500 --> 00:36:13.500
[Hande clears throat]

719
00:36:13.541 --> 00:36:16.625
A double shot macchiato
at 50 degrees with skim, no sugar. You?

720
00:36:17.833 --> 00:36:19.083
I don't really care. [chuckles]

721
00:36:21.125 --> 00:36:23.250
And a black sugar
strawberry milkshake please.

722
00:36:23.333 --> 00:36:24.375
[server] Coming right up.

723
00:36:25.416 --> 00:36:27.958
Don't ever say that you don't care.

724
00:36:28.041 --> 00:36:29.916
If you don't care about yourself...

725
00:36:30.666 --> 00:36:32.000
Why would anyone else care?

726
00:36:32.625 --> 00:36:33.750
Exactly. [chuckles]

727
00:36:33.833 --> 00:36:34.958
Mm-hmm.

728
00:36:40.958 --> 00:36:44.375
So do you know what's the first thing
men find attractive in a woman?

729
00:36:44.458 --> 00:36:45.500
Um, titties?

730
00:36:45.583 --> 00:36:46.750
PUT A SMILE ON

731
00:36:46.833 --> 00:36:47.833
Booty.

732
00:36:49.875 --> 00:36:50.708
Mnh-mnh.

733
00:36:50.791 --> 00:36:51.791
Hmm.

734
00:36:56.083 --> 00:36:59.208
- Ah, the smile. [laughs]
- Wonderful.

735
00:36:59.291 --> 00:37:01.625
Thankfully, yours is already great.

736
00:37:01.708 --> 00:37:04.875
But you need to learn how to look
in men's eyes when you smile at them.

737
00:37:05.541 --> 00:37:09.791
Because we reflect what the person
in front of us makes us feel.

738
00:37:09.875 --> 00:37:11.916
- [laughing]
- Good job.

739
00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:13.840
Come on,
you're good to go on out on the field.

740
00:37:13.875 --> 00:37:14.875
[Hande sighs, squeals]

741
00:37:17.875 --> 00:37:19.458
[players chattering]

742
00:37:19.541 --> 00:37:21.541
I thought that field thing
was metaphorical,

743
00:37:21.625 --> 00:37:24.625
but you really did bring me to a game.
How cool. [chuckles]

744
00:37:25.208 --> 00:37:29.250
Always try to stay in plain sight,
but you should never approach directly.

745
00:37:35.791 --> 00:37:36.791
[Hande] Oh.

746
00:37:37.666 --> 00:37:39.458
Okay, okay. He's coming here.

747
00:37:43.791 --> 00:37:44.791
Hmm.

748
00:37:46.083 --> 00:37:47.333
Oh! He looked at me. Oh!

749
00:37:47.916 --> 00:37:50.791
Welcome to his radar. [chuckles]

750
00:37:50.875 --> 00:37:52.875
[upbeat music playing]

751
00:37:52.958 --> 00:37:54.625
